cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Robust Latent-Drift Compensation with FTM Anchoring (Section 3.5 reference implementation)"
abstract: >-
  Single-file C++17 reference implementation of Section 3.5 (drift compensation
  and FTM anchoring of the radiomap) of a dissertation on hybrid Bayesian
  tactical spatial identification of Wi-Fi signal sources: latent-drift Kalman
  predict/update with a Huber robust step, immutable base radiomap,
  trusted-update gate separating quarantine from update, and EIG-based anchor
  selection. The Kalman gain is computed by a stable Cholesky solve.
type: software
